{
  "id": "two-failures-flake-and-type-error",
  "title": "Two failed jobs: an unrelated sandbox ECONNRESET and a type error the PR caused in untouched files",
  "description": "PR #241 makes User.email optional (phone-only signups) in src/models/user.ts. Two jobs fail. 'test' finishes first and is listed first: one integration test against the SMS provider's public sandbox fails with 'fetch failed' / read ECONNRESET (the 'Transient network error' signature), while all unit tests pass; the job's history on main shows the same job failing on 2 of the last 10 unrelated commits. 'typecheck' fails with three TS errors (TS2345, TS2322, TS18048) in files the PR did not touch (send-digest.ts, welcome.ts, unsubscribe.ts), all because user.email is now 'string | undefined'. A rerun can only fix the first failure; the run stays red until the type errors are fixed, so the actionable answer is category code, naming the optional email change. The third keyword group asks that the answer also account for the second failed job (the sandbox flake), with broad synonyms. No fixPath: the fix can go in user.ts or in the three call sites.",
